{
  "$comment": [
    "STEP 1: put your Alchemy key in .env at the repo root, without the alch_ prefix:",
    "          ALCHEMY_KEY=your-key-here",
    "        .env is gitignored, so the key never reaches a commit. This file is safe to push.",
    "STEP 2: npm run verify -- --no-quote -v",
    "",
    "${ALCHEMY_KEY} below is substituted from the environment at load time. A real shell",
    "export of the same name also works and takes precedence over .env.",
    "",
    "'@auto' expands to the endpoints resolved automatically (LayerZero metadata + chainlist).",
    "Every chain below is 'try Alchemy first, then fall back to public', so a slug Alchemy",
    "does not serve costs one failed DNS lookup and the chain still gets verified.",
    "",
    "Every endpoint is chain-id checked and eth_call-probed before use, so neither a wrong URL",
    "nor a provider that blocks contract reads can decide a chain's result - it is skipped",
    "and the next candidate is tried.",
    "",
    "SLUGS: chains marked (confirmed) come from the Network enum in alchemy-sdk-js.",
    "Chains marked (guessed) are not in that enum - the enum lags what Alchemy actually",
    "serves (stable-mainnet is live but absent from it), so they are worth attempting.",
    "Run with -v to see which endpoint each chain actually used."
  ],
  "$slugs": {
